    {
      "id": 151716,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-12-23T19:21:24.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"carnilius\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/d07c76/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> carnilius:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The wording on Santa Guise's incap side says \"Flip 1 face-down card\", not one face-down hero card. &nbsp;As far as I know, this is the only way to flip an arbitrary face down card. &nbsp;Certainly this can work advantageously against Guise's nemesis Wager Master as you can return a favorable condition card into play, but where else can this be used? &nbsp;Can you flip face down cards that are under other cards, like from La Capitan or Savage Mana?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Sure you could flip the cards over under la capitan or savage mana. but they are still \"under\" those other cards and would continue to not have text.</p>\n<p>The flip a card thing really is a call to his nemesis Wager Master. EmoSpite also has his drugs you could flip, though not sure why you would want to do that.</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:30:39.166Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
