    {
      "id": 151717,
      "name": "carnilius",
      "username": "carnilius",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/d07c76/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-12-23T19:26:06.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>carnilius wrote:</b><br><blockquote>The wording on Santa Guise's incap side says \"Flip 1 face-down card\", not one face-down hero card. &nbsp;As far as I know, this is the only way to flip an arbitrary face down card. &nbsp;Certainly this can work advantageously against Guise's nemesis Wager Master as you can return a favorable condition card into play, but where else can this be used? &nbsp;Can you flip face down cards that are under other cards, like from La Capitan or Savage Mana?\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nSure you could flip the cards over under la capitan or savage mana. but they are still \"under\" those other cards and would continue to not have text.The flip a card thing really is a call to his nemesis Wager Master. EmoSpite also has his drugs you could flip, though not sure why you would want to do that.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Except the full wording is \"Flip a face-down card, treating it as played\". &nbsp;That would mean that if you <em>could</em> flip cards underneath cards, then they would be played, and hence no longer under the card.</p>",
