      "raw": "[quote=\"Foote\"]\n\n&nbsp;\n<div class=\"bb-quote\"><b>carnilius wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class=\"bb-quote-body\">The wording on Santa Guise&#39;s incap side says &quot;Flip 1 face-down card&quot;, not one face-down hero card. &nbsp;As far as I know, this is the only way to flip an arbitrary face down card. &nbsp;Certainly this can work advantageously against Guise&#39;s nemesis Wager Master as you can return a favorable condition card into play, but where else can this be used? &nbsp;Can you flip face down cards that are under other cards, like from La Capitan or Savage Mana?\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nSure you could flip the cards over under la capitan or savage mana. but they are still &quot;under&quot; those other cards and would continue to not have text.The flip a card thing really is a call to his nemesis Wager Master. EmoSpite also has his drugs you could flip, though not sure why you would want to do that.\n\n[/quote]\n\nExcept the full wording is &quot;Flip a face-down card, treating it as played&quot;. &nbsp;That would mean that if you <em>could</em> flip cards underneath cards, then they would be played, and hence no longer under the card.\n",
