    {
      "id": 151718,
      "name": "Ronway",
      "username": "Ronway",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-12-23T19:31:46.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Sure you could flip the cards over under la capitan or savage mana. but they are still \"under\" those other cards and would continue to not have text.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Who says the cards under La Capitan or Savage Mana go there face-down? The way someone puts them under there is just personal preference, as the way they are put under other cards actually has no impact on the game. So I would say you would be unable to flip them face-up unless there is a place that specifically states cards under cards are face-down.</p>",
